  "id": "Compound::DB00188 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Bortezomib may be associated with Hematologic Cancer through a series of interconnected pathways. Bortezomib is linked to Ventricular Dysfunction, which is caused by either Dasatinib or Nilotinib, both of which are known to treat Hematologic Cancer. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Bortezomib could influence the development or progression of Hematologic Cancer, possibly through the effects of these drugs on cellular processes. The shared lowest common ancestor, Carboxamide, suggests a common biochemical pathway or structural feature that may underlie the observed relationships. The evidence is consistent with a role for Bortezomib in modulating cellular functions that contribute to Hematologic Cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, and further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Bortezomib and Hematologic Cancer.",
